config {
  type: "assertion",
  tags: ["cm360", "dv360", "monitoring"],
  description: "Fails if a Keboola staging window collapses to a handful of days. This is the guard on every mart that was switched from incremental append-only to a full rebuild on 2026-11-03 — a full rebuild of a one-day source writes a one-day mart and throws the history away."
}

-- An assertion FAILS if it returns rows. Empty result = healthy.
--
-- WHY THIS EXISTS.
-- Until 2026-11-03, fct_cm360_placement_hourly and fct_dv360_reach_daily
-- were incremental and append-only. That was not a performance choice:
-- on 2026-10-05 the Keboola extracts held ONE DAY at a time, and a full
-- rebuild had already wiped the history once. Append-only was the fix.
--
-- It had a cost. A date already loaded was never reloaded, so an
-- upstream RESTATEMENT was ignored forever. Measured 2026-11-03, that
-- cost 26,900 clicks and 589,778 impressions on CM360 across five days,
-- and 8.8M impressions on DV360 inventory. Clicks are attributed later
-- than impressions, so a date first loaded while Keboola was still
-- half-landed kept its impressions and lost most of its clicks.
--
-- The extracts now hold 34-44 days, so those marts were switched to full
-- rebuilds and the restatements come through.
--
-- THAT MAKES THIS ASSERTION THE SAFETY NET. If Keboola ever reverts to a
-- narrow window, the next rebuild silently replaces a month of history
-- with a day or two of it. Nothing else would notice: the tables would
-- be freshly built, every assertion on grain and nullability would pass,
-- and assert_source_freshness checks the LATEST date, not how many there
-- are -- a one-day extract carrying yesterday looks perfectly fresh.
--
-- The marts that depend on this assertion are skipped when it fails,
-- which is the point: better a stale mart than a destroyed one.
--
-- stg_cm360_reach matters most of the three. Since 2026-11-03 it is
-- where core.fct_ad_performance_daily gets CM360 CLICKS from -- the
-- placement-level reports undercount them by about 65% -- so a
-- collapsed window there does not just thin a table, it takes the
-- channel's headline click figure with it.
--
-- THE THRESHOLD is 7 days, well below the 34-44 these windows currently
-- carry and well above the 1 that caused the original incident. It is
-- deliberately not tuned close to today's value -- a window shrinking
-- from 35 days to 20 is worth knowing about but is not an emergency,
-- while a drop to 1 or 2 destroys data on the next run.

WITH windows AS (
  SELECT 'stg_cm360_hourly' AS sursa, COUNT(DISTINCT date) AS zile
  FROM ${ref("stg_cm360_hourly")}
  WHERE date IS NOT NULL

  UNION ALL
  SELECT 'stg_cm360_reach', COUNT(DISTINCT date)
  FROM ${ref("stg_cm360_reach")}
  WHERE date IS NOT NULL

  UNION ALL
  SELECT 'stg_dv360_reach', COUNT(DISTINCT date)
  FROM ${ref("stg_dv360_reach")}
  WHERE date IS NOT NULL
)
SELECT
  sursa,
  zile,
  7 AS prag,
  'Keboola window collapsed. A full rebuild of this source will destroy history — switch the dependent marts back to incremental BEFORE the next run.' AS actiune
FROM windows
WHERE zile < 7
